From 88de7deef8a24a1c48eac53fcd825cadced6394b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RDoom <171243930+aeon1911@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:09:54 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 42/60] Switch: smoke area budget under the stabilizer, no SD
 access or cache readback in frames

HW test of 8cf03687d: in fights the stabilizer sat at its top level and the
smoke still had 188 translucent sprites per frame, 58% of the frames late,
9.6 ms of 3D scene on the GPU at 60% resolution: the smoke is close and
dense, so faint/distant culling cannot help. BeginFrame "save" still took
67-83 ms three times.

- Translucent effects (never players, monsters, projectiles, pickups or
  shootable things) get a screen area budget while the stabilizer is active
  (20 screens at level 1 down to 3 at level 6, nx_effect_area overrides):
  sprites are processed near to far, so the smoke behind smoke goes first.
- WarmFilename is computed once per run: M_GetCachePath(true) creates the
  directory on the SD card on every list save.
- The pipeline cache data is read on a worker (65-85 ms on the Switch);
  pipeline creation and the readback share a mutex.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
